Contributors to zpaq-std
========================

This file lists the people who have contributed code, ideas, or substantial
work to this fork of zpaq-std.

Maintainer
----------
- YadeWira (Yade Bravo) <https://github.com/YadeWira>
  Creator and sole maintainer of this fork (YadeWira/zpaq-std).
  Owns the `-ma:algo:N` switch family, the bundled-compressors architecture
  (compressors/), the Makefile, the 32-bit `m32` build target, the
  MinGW-w64 Windows 7+ cross-compile, README.md, and WORKFLOW.md.


Upstream lineage (acknowledgements, not contributors to this fork)
------------------------------------------------------------------
- Matt Mahoney — original author of zpaq 7.15 (2009–2016), the deduplicated
  journaling archiver at the root of the zpaq family tree. <http://mattmahoney.net/zpaq.html>
- Franco Corbelli — author of `zpaqfranz` (this fork's direct ancestor) and
  of `zpaq-std` (a sibling fork of the same name). Both forks added
  production features (HW acceleration, SFX, SFTP, FRANZEN, etc.) on top
  of Mahoney's zpaq 7.15 and kept the codebase as a single C++ file.
  See https://github.com/fcorbelli/zpaqfranz and https://github.com/fcorbelli/zpaq-std.
- The `compressors/` directory contains verbatim source code from:
    * LZ4 by Yann Collet
    * zstd by Yann Collet / Meta
    * fast-lzma2 by Conor McCarthy
    * LZ5 by Przemysław Skibinski / Simon Hahne / Paul Sanja-Luminari
    * Lizard by Przemysław Skibinski
    * bzip2 by Julian Seward
    * bzip3 by Kamila Szewczyk
    * brotli by Google (Jyrki Alakuijala, et al.)
    * Snappy by Google (Jyrki Alakuijala, et al.) — BSD-3
    * libdeflate by Eric Biggers (ebiggers) — MIT
    * lzlib by Antonio Diaz Diaz and the lzip maintainers — BSD-2
    * LZAV by Aleksey Vaneev (avaneev) — MIT
    * heatshrink by Scott Vokes (atomicobject) — ISC
    * LZFSE by Apple Inc. — BSD-3
    * zopfli KrzYmod by Mr_KrzYch00 (fork of google/zopfli) — Apache-2.0
    * libbsc by Ilya Grebnov — Apache-2.0
    * LZHAM by Rich Geldreich (richgel999) — Public Domain
  Each library keeps its original copyright and license. See the individual
  source files in compressors/ for details.

This fork began from the public repository at https://github.com/fcorbelli/zpaqfranz
(the `zpaqfranz.cpp` file was renamed to `zpaq-std.cpp` as part of the fork,
but the source code itself is Franco Corbelli's). It is a derivative work
in the spirit of the MIT license, with substantial new code by YadeWira
(the bundled-compressors architecture, the 18-algorithm `ma:` switch
family, the 32-bit Linux build, the Windows 7+ cross-compile, the test
infrastructure, and the documentation).
